b.constraint('graph_function_template_and_reuse',['graph_function'],'Template is replayable publication truth. HoG-local resolution is invocation convenience only, not the published contract or substitute program. Named work reuse uses GraphFunctions, not copied structures or Product shells. GraphFunction is the composition/substitution/recursion/HOF unit, and outer contract stays stable across internal refinement.',[(0,21,24),(0,30,34)])
b.constraint('graph_function_publication_surfaces',['graph_function'],'Effects support static analysis, capability matching, lawful composition and workflow visibility. declarations canonically carries publication/materialization metadata, dispatch/evaluation/escalation/proof/closure/assurance hook references, opaque hook config and local publication surfaces. Publish discoverable first-class module surfaces, not anonymous realized graphs or helper code.',[(0,28,28),(0,36,38)])
b.constraint('materialization_identity',['graph_function'],'Expose which GraphFunction materialized, the declared input/parameter basis and resulting graph identity/provenance. Every callable publishes a template whose materialized graph passes GTL validation and is directly HoG-traversable. Implementation bindings realize only declared leaf seams. Reject implementation-only handlers/plugins/Workers/pointers claiming GraphFunction identity without matching template, graph, contracts, program membership and provenance.',[(0,40,40),(0,88,96)])
b.latitude('materialization_latitude',['graph_function'],['Depend on declared inputs, selected workflow families and declared structural parameters.','Derive companion bundles if Graph stays primary output and derivation has replayable provenance.','Cache/reuse only under declared materialization-input plus GraphFunction identity.','Realize one or more internal GraphVector boundaries.'],['Relying on hidden ambient interpreter/process state for materialization or cache identity.','Treating HoG-local resolution as a substitute executable program.'],[(0,21,26),(0,42,48)])
b.constraint('callable_identity_partition',['graph_function','graph_vector'],'GraphFunction is the public work entry for semantic Jobs and other starts; bare vectors are not callable. Realized vectors remain subordinate structure. The callable is distinct from materialized Graph and ABG graph-call instance and is not the whole Program, attempt, workspace, overlay or downstream asset. A Program/overlay composition instead binds callables, vectors, node types, starts, roles, security, policy, proofs and plugin/result contracts.',[(0,46,48),(0,56,60),(0,82,86)])
b.constraint('graph_function_environment_consistency',['graph_function','cumulative_environment'],'Keep environment explicit and immutable with requires/provides/carries; require inputs=requires and outputs represented in provides. After lawful execution, carries conserves upstream required bindings and new outputs.',[(0,50,54)])
